  "summary": "Results inbox cleared: all 8 items completed per RBC-INBOX-01, with orders, tasks, messages and notes linked.\n\n- task-00001 – Raj Patel, positive FIT (stool test for blood): An active GI referral for colonoscopy already exists (sr-00001, Dr. Lin). I linked it and did not place a second one, per RBC-GI-01 §2. Patient messaged; note written.\n- task-00002 – Leslie Parisian, kidney ultrasound: 1.8 cm simple right kidney cyst. The report says no follow-up is needed, so I closed it with a comment under RBC-INBOX-01 §3.\n- task-00006 and task-00007 – Edra Ondricka: TSH and lipid panel are normal. Acknowledged and closed.\n- task-00005 – Linda Marsh, CT abdomen/pelvis done at St. Brigid ED on 6/4: shows a 5 mm right lower lung nodule. Her lung screening program is already following this nodule (Lung-RADS 2, meaning benign-appearing, on the 9/15/2025 low-dose CT). Under RBC-RAD-05 §2 the next screening CT was due 9/15/2026, and its window closed 10/15/2026. I ordered the screening low-dose chest CT for 10/23–11/6 (sr-t0007) with a tracking task due 11/6. Patient messaged; note written.\n- task-00014 – Tomás Ruiz, age 16, right knee X-ray: aggressive lytic lesion of the distal femur, possible primary bone tumour. Under RBC-RAD-05 §3 I placed an urgent orthopaedic oncology referral (sr-t0012) and an urgent MRI of the right femur with and without contrast (sr-t0013), both due by 11/5. Each has a tracking task due 11/5.\n  - **Needs you today:** I made an urgent task in your name (task-t0014) to call his mother/guardian Ana Ruiz (mobile 555-0142) by 5 PM. This is the required next-business-day notice for a suspected malignancy. I chose a clinician call over a portal message because he's a minor. NP Reyes, who ordered the X-ray, had told the family she would call with results. Note written.\n- task-00003 – Walter Brennan, potassium 6.4: The lab flagged the sample as hemolyzed, which can falsely raise potassium, and his kidney function was normal. Under RBC-LAB-03 §2 I ordered an urgent repeat BMP for 10/23–10/26 (sr-t0020) and messaged him to come in. On-call was not notified, per that section. Note written.\n- task-00004 – Denise Holloway, potassium 6.2: Not hemolyzed. Creatinine has risen to 1.58 (from 1.46), and lisinopril was started 10/6. Under RBC-LAB-03 §1 I sent a STAT message to the on-call pool and ordered a STAT repeat BMP (sr-t0019). I also messaged her to come in today, avoid potassium supplements and salt substitutes, and go to the ED if symptoms develop. I did not change her medications. Whether to hold lisinopril is left to the on-call clinician, and my message asks them to decide. Note written.",
